        "original_id": "7516362e-2750-532a-aa7a-fd6e334afc1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah National Park, Virginia, Rappahannock County, Culpeper County, Chesapeake Bay\n- Rivers: Hazel River, Covington River, Rappahannock River\n- Organizations: U.S. National Park System\n- Topics: Blue Ridge Mountains, river systems\n\nFacts:\n- Shenandoah National Park is a national park in Virginia that encompasses part of the Blue Ridge Mountains.\n- The Hazel River rises in Shenandoah National Park.\n- The Hazel River flows generally eastward through Rappahannock County and Culpeper County.\n- The Covington River system flows via the Hazel River to the Rappahannock River.\n- The Rappahannock River is a tributary of Chesapeake Bay.",
